  "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nWhen adding 'Media Release' item for an existing emby integration, the following error is received. \n\nTRPCClientError: An unknown error occured while executing Integration method\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nFrom Dashboard \n\n+ New Item\n\nSearch and add a 'Media Releases' item\n<img width=\"193\" height=\"216\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b06f95b3-0a16-4cd8-be85-4f06570607ae\" />\n\nEdit the new item and select Emby\n<img width=\"641\" height=\"413\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4f007919-b92c-48f8-87e7-c28ed4a548b5\" />\n\nSave Changes\n<img width=\"322\" height=\"329\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5cd37435-7460-4f2e-83f4-38bf2099f3e6\" />\n\n### Impact\n\nThe dashboard item does not retrieve newly added items to the dashboard, instead provides the error above.  \n\nHomarr is not impacted in any other noticeable way. \n\n### Additional information\n\n> 2025-10-26T20:52:11.452Z error: tRPC Error with query on 'widget.mediaRelease.getMediaReleases' \n>     at Object.onError (/app/apps/nextjs/.next/server/app/api/trpc/[trpc]/route.js:5:5500)\n>     at Object.onError (/app/apps/nextjs/.next/server/app/api/trpc/[trpc]/route.js:5:4124)\n>     at /app/apps/nextjs/.next/server/app/api/trpc/[trpc]/route.js:1:31608\n>     at process.processTicksAndRejections (node:internal/process/task_queues:105:5)\n>     at async /app/apps/nextjs/.next/server/app/api/trpc/[trpc]/route.js:5:1384\n> caused by Error: An unknown error occured while executing Integration method integrationId=\"j5ql99ql1hrwvgo56dpr9bb1\" integrationName=\"Emby\" integrationUrl=\"http://192.168.1.148:8096\"\n>     at c (/app/apps/nextjs/.next/server/chunks/8950.js:6:79121)\n>     at /app/apps/nextjs/.next/server/chunks/8950.js:6:79233\n>     at process.processTicksAndRejections (node:internal/process/task_queues:105:5)\n>     at async Object.requestAsync (/app/apps/nextjs/.next/server/chunks/8950.js:6:208968)\n>     at async Object.requestAsync (/app/apps/nextjs/.next/server/chunks/8950.js:135:17968)\n>     at async g (/app/apps/nextjs/.next/server/chunks/8950.js:5:23890)\n>     at async Object.getCachedOrUpdatedDataAsync (/app/apps/nextjs/.next/server/chunks/8950.js:5:24358)\n>     at async /app/apps/nextjs/.next/server/chunks/8950.js:6:12565\n>     at async Promise.all (index 0)\n>     at async /app/apps/nextjs/.next/server/chunks/8950.js:6:12473\n> caused by Error: No users found \n>     at p.getMediaReleasesAsync (/app/apps/nextjs/.next/server/chunks/8950.js:6:47547)\n>     at process.processTicksAndRejections (node:internal/process/task_queues:105:5)\n>     at async Object.requestAsync (/app/apps/nextjs/.next/server/chunks/8950.js:6:208968)\n>     at async Object.requestAsync (/app/apps/nextjs/.next/server/chunks/8950.js:135:17968)\n>     at async g (/app/apps/nextjs/.next/server/chunks/8950.js:5:23890)\n>     at async Object.getCachedOrUpdatedDataAsync (/app/apps/nextjs/.next/server/chunks/8950.js:5:24358)\n>     at async /app/apps/nextjs/.next/server/chunks/8950.js:6:12565\n>     at async Promise.all (index 0)\n>     at async /app/apps/nextjs/.next/server/chunks/8950.js:6:12473\n>     at async u.middlewares (/app/apps/nextjs/.next/server/chunks/2032.js:232:166456)\n\nreviewing the logs indicates that there is no user found.\n\n### Version\n\n1.43.0\n\n### Installation method\n\nUnraid Apps\n\n### Browser\n\nFirefox\n\n### Notes\n\nIt should be possible to select the user for which the library and latest medias should be fetched from. For this we probably could use the dynamic select added in #2645 ",
